WEBVTT

00:00:19.490 --> 00:00:26.750
<i>New days, it's the morning we begin. 
Let's give the world a kiss.</i>

00:00:27.710 --> 00:00:35.240
<i>Blowing in the wind, with a little 
courage and love in our pockets.</i>

00:00:37.140 --> 00:00:44.090
<i>I wish: If only I had wings,</i>

00:00:45.390 --> 00:00:53.690
<i>I could fly over the sadness, 
the past, and my doubts.</i>

00:00:53.690 --> 00:01:02.450
<i>Oh, yeah! There's nothing to lose. 
(Take whatever the brand new day brings.)</i>

00:01:02.450 --> 00:01:07.290
<i>Take my way! I wanna catch a miracle...</i>

00:01:07.290 --> 00:01:11.030
<i>in the palm of my hand!</i>

00:01:11.800 --> 00:01:19.720
<i>We're off on a journey through the endless 
earth, the skies, and the future.</i>

00:01:20.290 --> 00:01:32.140
<i>I know these newborn wings, oh! 
Are gonna gonna gonna shine someday!</i>

00:01:34.360 --> 00:01:35.780
We're leaving here right now.

00:01:36.900 --> 00:01:39.160
Looks like they're onto us.

00:01:39.160 --> 00:01:40.780
He probably saw your face, too.

00:01:40.780 --> 00:01:42.990
Why did you even open the door?!

00:01:42.990 --> 00:01:44.750
If I hadn't, he would have broken it down.

00:01:45.500 --> 00:01:48.710
He's probably calling for 
reinforcements right about now.

00:01:48.710 --> 00:01:50.710
Once they meet up with him, 
they'll storm the place.

00:01:51.210 --> 00:01:53.140
We can't stay here any longer.

00:01:55.970 --> 00:01:57.170
You're kidding...

00:01:57.170 --> 00:01:58.630
Why's this happening?

00:02:06.470 --> 00:02:08.480
What're you doing? Hurry up!

00:02:08.480 --> 00:02:09.520
Um... Right.

00:02:11.520 --> 00:02:12.980
Open up! We're the Royal Forces!

00:02:12.980 --> 00:02:14.560
Open the door!

00:02:16.360 --> 00:02:17.820
One, two...

00:02:25.500 --> 00:02:26.700
What <i>is </i>this place?

00:02:26.700 --> 00:02:27.860
Beats me.

00:02:27.860 --> 00:02:29.750
Looks like it's been here 
a long time, though.

00:02:29.750 --> 00:02:32.460
You knew about this place all along?

00:02:32.460 --> 00:02:33.210
Yeah.

00:02:34.670 --> 00:02:39.720
"Back Alley Elegy"

00:02:49.810 --> 00:02:50.600
What's the matter?

00:02:53.230 --> 00:02:54.570
This is a playhouse, isn't it?

00:02:55.190 --> 00:02:57.770
An amusement center where 
humans escape into fantasy.

00:02:58.490 --> 00:03:02.530
I bet Cin would've enjoyed it.

00:03:04.990 --> 00:03:06.370
What, again?

00:03:07.120 --> 00:03:09.830
Somebody was in here yesterday 
asking the same thing.

00:03:09.830 --> 00:03:12.960
Wanted to know if there was a 
blonde girl with blue eyes here.

00:03:12.960 --> 00:03:15.960
Did she break the law or something?

00:03:15.960 --> 00:03:17.550
Shut your mouth.

00:03:18.550 --> 00:03:20.010
Don't worry.

00:03:20.690 --> 00:03:23.000
They've still got their patrols going around.

00:03:23.490 --> 00:03:26.100
She wasn't hauled away by the Royal Forces.

00:03:26.100 --> 00:03:27.970
But where in the world did she go?

00:03:27.970 --> 00:03:30.020
She'll be okay.

00:03:30.020 --> 00:03:34.400
C'mon, that boy looked like he had 
a good head on his shoulders, right?

00:03:34.400 --> 00:03:35.440
I suppose you're right...

00:03:35.980 --> 00:03:38.400
Anyway, they might come back here,

00:03:38.850 --> 00:03:40.840
so let's wait a while longer.

00:03:48.330 --> 00:03:49.880
Parabellum?

00:03:51.500 --> 00:03:53.500
Parabellum!

00:03:53.500 --> 00:03:56.130
What in the world are you doing here?

00:03:56.130 --> 00:03:58.720
I thought I left you at an inn...

00:03:58.720 --> 00:03:59.920
Who are you?

00:03:59.920 --> 00:04:00.460
Sir?

00:04:00.460 --> 00:04:03.430
This area's off-limits except 
to authorized personnel.

00:04:03.430 --> 00:04:05.430
If you've got no business 
here, then clear out!

00:04:05.430 --> 00:04:08.930
Well, the thing is, this horse is my...

00:04:09.810 --> 00:04:10.900
Your what?

00:04:11.600 --> 00:04:14.940
N-No, it's nothing!

00:04:18.940 --> 00:04:20.570
What do you mean, you can't find them?!

00:04:21.780 --> 00:04:23.320
We've cut their mobility by confiscating

00:04:23.320 --> 00:04:25.360
every horse in the capital 
with an unknown owner!

00:04:25.360 --> 00:04:27.620
We've also doubled our patrols!

00:04:27.620 --> 00:04:30.120
They have to be lying low somewhere!

00:04:30.120 --> 00:04:32.540
Find them, no matter what 
it takes! Is that clear?

00:04:33.080 --> 00:04:35.170
The future of the kingdom depends on it!

00:04:35.170 --> 00:04:35.920
Yes, sir!

00:04:41.920 --> 00:04:43.920
Boy, this really puts us in a bind.

00:04:43.920 --> 00:04:46.930
I can't believe that Miss Winia 
and I are wanted fugitives, too.

00:04:47.430 --> 00:04:49.600
Plus, they said that someone was just here,

00:04:49.600 --> 00:04:52.930
asking if they'd seen a 
blonde girl with blue eyes.

00:04:52.930 --> 00:04:55.890
There's a good chance we'll be 
caught even if we stay down here.

00:04:55.890 --> 00:04:59.650
At any rate, we need to get out of 
the capital as soon as possible.

00:04:59.650 --> 00:05:02.360
Look, there's one thing that 
I really don't understand.

00:05:02.710 --> 00:05:04.450
Why do I have to run away,

00:05:04.450 --> 00:05:06.570
just because I'm the Scrapped 
Princess or whatever?

00:05:06.570 --> 00:05:07.820
What do you mean?

00:05:08.200 --> 00:05:09.540
It doesn't make sense.

00:05:09.540 --> 00:05:11.410
I'm a princess, right?

00:05:11.410 --> 00:05:13.620
Why do they have to take me prisoner?!

00:05:13.620 --> 00:05:16.870
To the kingdom, you represent 
a serious threat.

00:05:16.870 --> 00:05:19.840
Why? What's so threatening about me?

00:05:19.840 --> 00:05:21.550
Beats me.

00:05:21.550 --> 00:05:23.340
But the Church of Mauser says

00:05:23.340 --> 00:05:26.670
that the Scrapped Princess will 
bring devastation to the world.

00:05:28.340 --> 00:05:30.200
If I had stayed in the military,

00:05:30.200 --> 00:05:32.260
I'd probably be hunting you, too.

00:05:33.310 --> 00:05:35.330
You used to be a soldier?

00:05:40.070 --> 00:05:40.820
What's wrong?

00:05:40.820 --> 00:05:42.440
You took the egg!

00:05:42.440 --> 00:05:44.780
There are plenty of eggs left in there.

00:05:44.780 --> 00:05:46.710
But that one was cooked just how I like it,

00:05:46.710 --> 00:05:48.450
so I was about to grab it!

00:05:48.450 --> 00:05:50.740
Gimme a break... Grab another one!

00:05:50.740 --> 00:05:53.740
You haven't bitten into 
it yet, so give it to me!

00:05:53.740 --> 00:05:54.600
Forget it!

00:05:54.600 --> 00:05:55.620
Um, Miss Pacifica?

00:05:55.620 --> 00:05:56.160
Pamela!

00:05:57.620 --> 00:06:00.040
Miss Pamela... If you like, you're 
more than welcome to mine.

00:06:00.040 --> 00:06:02.340
You took that one out too early.

00:06:02.340 --> 00:06:04.800
The outside needs to be browner.

00:06:04.800 --> 00:06:06.630
That's why I want <i>that </i>one!

00:06:06.630 --> 00:06:07.670
Give it a rest!

00:06:07.670 --> 00:06:09.590
The corn's done!

00:06:09.590 --> 00:06:11.640
I'm sorry, Keydarf.

00:06:11.640 --> 00:06:13.250
Not only are we having you hide us,

00:06:13.250 --> 00:06:15.060
but imposing on you for dinner, too...

00:06:15.060 --> 00:06:16.580
It's fine, it's fine.

00:06:16.580 --> 00:06:18.060
Don't worry about it.

00:06:18.060 --> 00:06:19.600
If you make too much noise, though,

00:06:19.600 --> 00:06:20.850
the proprietor will get mad at me.

00:06:20.850 --> 00:06:22.310
I said hand it over!

00:06:22.310 --> 00:06:23.480
And I said no way!

00:06:23.480 --> 00:06:24.450
Give it!

00:06:24.450 --> 00:06:25.780
Quiet down, you two!

00:06:26.530 --> 00:06:28.450
What's this all about, Chris?

00:06:28.450 --> 00:06:31.320
We know where the Scrapped 
Princess is hiding,

00:06:31.320 --> 00:06:33.130
so why aren't we moving on the place?

00:06:33.760 --> 00:06:35.560
Now, now, just wait.

00:06:36.010 --> 00:06:39.500
I'm sure that our little Chris 
has something up his sleeve.

00:06:39.500 --> 00:06:41.250
Well, do you, Chris?

00:06:41.250 --> 00:06:42.000
I'm sorry.

00:06:42.450 --> 00:06:45.460
But to tell you the truth, 
I just don't know anymore.

00:06:45.460 --> 00:06:48.260
I'm not sure if handing 
the Scrapped Princess over

00:06:48.260 --> 00:06:50.430
to the kingdom is the right thing to do.

00:06:50.430 --> 00:06:55.430
But if we don't do something, the 
Obstinate Arrows will be disbanded.

00:06:56.700 --> 00:06:59.770
What'll happen to us if we have to leave?

00:07:01.150 --> 00:07:03.400
Come on, Sutton, don't cry.

00:07:03.860 --> 00:07:05.860
I'm not crying!

00:07:07.230 --> 00:07:11.950
The thing is, if everybody in 
the kingdom wants to kill me,

00:07:11.950 --> 00:07:15.660
how far will we have to go before we're safe?

00:07:15.660 --> 00:07:17.790
Is there a place I can be safe?

00:07:19.960 --> 00:07:23.390
Um... What if we went to the Giat Empire?

00:07:23.390 --> 00:07:26.900
Then we wouldn't have to worry about 
the Royal Forces chasing us, right?

00:07:27.960 --> 00:07:29.720
That might've been true earlier,

00:07:29.720 --> 00:07:32.180
but relations between us 
and Giat are strained now

00:07:32.180 --> 00:07:35.220
because of the Ginnungagap incident 
on the coast of the capital.

00:07:35.220 --> 00:07:37.510
It'd be more dangerous to 
leave the country right now.

00:07:39.290 --> 00:07:43.230
Young lady, how about going to Grendel?

00:07:43.230 --> 00:07:44.590
Grendel?

00:07:44.590 --> 00:07:48.030
You mean the Grendel that's the main 
temple of the Church of Mauser?!

00:07:48.030 --> 00:07:50.490
It's inside Leinwan territory,

00:07:50.490 --> 00:07:53.450
but that's the one region 
that's totally autonomous.

00:07:54.110 --> 00:08:00.410
Even troops of the Royal Forces are strictly 
limited in the weapons they can carry.

00:08:00.910 --> 00:08:03.120
And I don't think that the Royal Forces

00:08:03.120 --> 00:08:05.880
would ever expect you 
to go to Grendel, right?

00:08:06.460 --> 00:08:09.130
I've heard that the Purgers, the 
combat unit that reports directly

00:08:09.130 --> 00:08:11.220
to the Church of Mauser, are 
headquartered in Grendel.

00:08:11.220 --> 00:08:15.340
Still, it's better than going up against 
the entire Royal Forces, isn't it?

00:08:18.580 --> 00:08:20.330
Um, guys?

00:08:20.330 --> 00:08:22.100
I feel like I should apologize.

00:08:23.230 --> 00:08:26.260
I don't really understand any of this,

00:08:26.260 --> 00:08:28.020
but you're risking so much for me.

00:08:28.020 --> 00:08:29.940
What're you talking about?

00:08:29.940 --> 00:08:31.530
Now that it's turned out like this,

00:08:31.940 --> 00:08:33.880
what else could we do?

00:08:35.070 --> 00:08:35.990
I'm sorry...

00:08:35.990 --> 00:08:39.620
Miss Raquel must be worried sick about us.

00:08:39.620 --> 00:08:42.080
If we all disappeared, she'd...

00:08:42.080 --> 00:08:44.790
Oh, that scary lady is in the capital, too?

00:08:44.790 --> 00:08:46.000
Yes.

00:08:46.000 --> 00:08:47.690
If only I'd asked what inn

00:08:47.690 --> 00:08:50.830
they were staying at when I 
met them at the food stand...

00:08:51.490 --> 00:08:54.200
Could we afford to put off 
our departure a while longer?

00:08:55.150 --> 00:08:56.990
It's okay. Let's go.

00:08:56.990 --> 00:08:59.430
If we wait around, we'll all be caught.

00:09:01.430 --> 00:09:04.480
If I see her, I'll be sure to tell her.

00:09:04.480 --> 00:09:06.350
Either way, we're going to need horses.

00:09:06.770 --> 00:09:08.310
Going on foot is out of the question.

00:09:08.310 --> 00:09:10.140
But from what Leo says,

00:09:10.140 --> 00:09:12.190
security is awfully tight.

00:09:12.190 --> 00:09:14.320
There's always gaps in any defense.

00:09:14.320 --> 00:09:17.530
I agree that we'll need to steal some horses.

00:09:17.530 --> 00:09:19.780
But what if we're spotted 
on our way to steal them?

00:09:20.120 --> 00:09:21.430
That's true...

00:09:22.320 --> 00:09:23.750
Why not use disguises?

00:09:24.090 --> 00:09:25.590
Yeah, this is the one!

00:09:25.590 --> 00:09:28.380
You've gotta go with a revealing 
one like this, Winia!

00:09:28.380 --> 00:09:29.750
Oh, but I...

00:09:40.140 --> 00:09:41.560
What's with you?

00:09:41.560 --> 00:09:42.720
Excuse me?

00:09:42.720 --> 00:09:44.060
You have something you want to say?

00:09:47.940 --> 00:09:51.020
Is Miss Pamela important to you, too?

00:09:51.570 --> 00:09:53.830
Important enough for you to 
risk your life to protect her?

00:09:54.740 --> 00:09:56.320
What's gotten into you?

00:09:56.320 --> 00:09:57.890
I mean, here you are,

00:09:57.890 --> 00:10:03.060
protecting someone that the entire 
country wants dead, right?

00:10:03.700 --> 00:10:05.000
If you put it that way, I guess I am...

00:10:06.370 --> 00:10:08.560
Maybe it's a conditioned 
response or something...

00:10:09.840 --> 00:10:13.460
In my job, I kept letting people go 
who were on the run or in trouble.

00:10:15.210 --> 00:10:17.260
Is that the only reason?

00:10:17.260 --> 00:10:17.970
What's it to you?

00:10:19.330 --> 00:10:20.680
What do you mean?

00:10:21.430 --> 00:10:24.310
Well, it sounds like she's 
important enough to you

00:10:24.310 --> 00:10:27.560
to be willing to throw away everything 
that matters to you to protect her.

00:10:29.350 --> 00:10:31.480
I don't know if you're an 
apprentice knight or whatever,

00:10:31.480 --> 00:10:33.900
but you'll never be a knight now.

00:10:33.900 --> 00:10:35.280
Why not?!

00:10:35.280 --> 00:10:36.780
What do you think?

00:10:36.780 --> 00:10:38.950
Properly speaking, your duty is to cut off

00:10:38.950 --> 00:10:40.660
the Scrapped Princess' head 
and bring it in, isn't it?

00:10:43.490 --> 00:10:45.620
You think that striking people 
down is all a knight is good for?

00:10:46.580 --> 00:10:49.460
I don't think that's true.

00:10:50.020 --> 00:10:51.080
I have to believe that it isn't.

00:10:55.260 --> 00:10:56.550
Thanks for waiting!

00:10:57.460 --> 00:10:58.870
So, how do I look?

00:11:00.030 --> 00:11:01.330
Is something wrong?

00:11:02.050 --> 00:11:03.010
Not really.

00:11:03.010 --> 00:11:04.550
Well?

00:11:05.220 --> 00:11:05.970
Nice.

00:11:05.970 --> 00:11:08.890
You could at least say 
something nice about it!

00:11:08.890 --> 00:11:10.940
Oh, golly. It's so wonderful.

00:11:11.400 --> 00:11:12.350
Fine, see if I care!

00:11:12.350 --> 00:11:13.900
What's the point in showing off to you?

00:11:15.320 --> 00:11:16.900
What're you doing?

00:11:16.900 --> 00:11:18.360
Oh, we're looking for disguises.

00:11:18.730 --> 00:11:20.840
We've already picked yours out.

00:11:21.490 --> 00:11:22.610
Ta-dah!

00:11:24.530 --> 00:11:26.540
Resistance is useless!

00:11:30.630 --> 00:11:32.250
Maybe he needs more makeup...

00:11:32.250 --> 00:11:33.580
Say what, you bitch?!

00:11:51.010 --> 00:11:52.310
You're so cute!

00:11:52.310 --> 00:11:53.680
It's not just flattery.

00:11:53.680 --> 00:11:55.730
It really does suit you.

00:11:55.730 --> 00:11:57.610
I don't care how struck by my beauty 
you are, I ain't happy about this.

00:11:57.610 --> 00:12:01.030
Hey, girls don't talk in 
that rough tone of voice!

00:12:01.030 --> 00:12:03.490
You're the last person who 
should be saying that.

00:12:03.490 --> 00:12:04.960
Oh, shut up.

00:12:04.960 --> 00:12:06.950
When a lady tells you to 
do something, you do it.

00:12:06.950 --> 00:12:08.580
Are you qualified?

00:12:08.580 --> 00:12:09.410
Hush, you!

00:12:16.920 --> 00:12:18.470
Hey, wait a minute!

00:12:19.130 --> 00:12:19.940
Hey!

00:12:22.340 --> 00:12:23.400
This way!

00:12:29.810 --> 00:12:32.480
We'll go steal some horses,

00:12:32.480 --> 00:12:34.390
so you two wait here.

00:12:34.390 --> 00:12:35.730
You're not gonna do it in drag?

00:12:35.730 --> 00:12:37.230
You're no fun...

00:12:37.230 --> 00:12:39.150
How are we supposed to move in those things?

00:12:39.150 --> 00:12:41.610
You better come back here without 
getting hurt, understand?

00:12:41.610 --> 00:12:43.570
Sure, don't worry about me.

00:12:43.570 --> 00:12:45.780
Who said I was worried?

00:12:45.780 --> 00:12:48.580
If you get hurt, it'll make lots 
of work for the rest of us.

00:12:48.580 --> 00:12:50.040
You know, bandaging you and stuff.

00:12:50.040 --> 00:12:51.870
I didn't think of that.

00:12:51.870 --> 00:12:55.170
Anyway, I don't want to see so 
much as a scratch on you, got it?

00:12:55.170 --> 00:12:57.630
As you wish, Highness.

00:12:57.630 --> 00:12:59.570
That <i>hurt</i>, you little twerp!

00:12:59.570 --> 00:13:01.000
You give it your best, too, Leo.

00:13:01.330 --> 00:13:02.460
Thank you.

00:13:09.330 --> 00:13:11.190
Um, Miss Pamela...

00:13:11.190 --> 00:13:11.930
Yeah?

00:13:12.630 --> 00:13:14.890
I... I'll keep you safe, so don't worry.

00:13:16.330 --> 00:13:19.440
I realize that I may still 
seem unreliable right now,

00:13:19.440 --> 00:13:22.530
but no one wishes to protect 
you more than I do.

00:13:22.530 --> 00:13:23.900
No one.

00:13:25.700 --> 00:13:27.340
Well, we're off!

00:13:28.950 --> 00:13:30.270
See you soon!

00:13:46.870 --> 00:13:49.410
Leo sure seemed manly, didn't he?

00:13:50.140 --> 00:13:51.530
It surprises you,

00:13:51.530 --> 00:13:53.940
hearing stuff like that out of the blue...

00:13:53.940 --> 00:13:55.560
So, what do you think?

00:13:56.140 --> 00:13:57.860
About Leo.

00:13:58.980 --> 00:14:00.860
I'm flattered that he feels that way,

00:14:00.860 --> 00:14:04.110
but, well, doesn't he seem kinda 
like a spoiled rich boy to you?

00:14:04.110 --> 00:14:07.070
Yes, well, he <i>is </i>nobility.

00:14:07.070 --> 00:14:08.490
Oh, I didn't know.

00:14:08.490 --> 00:14:10.990
Anyway, I think he's a 
nice guy and all, but...

00:14:10.990 --> 00:14:13.080
You like Furet better?

00:14:13.080 --> 00:14:15.000
What makes you say that?!

00:14:15.000 --> 00:14:16.850
Don't you?

00:14:16.850 --> 00:14:19.490
No way. I think he's...

00:14:19.490 --> 00:14:21.540
I don't really feel anything 
one way or the other.

00:14:26.320 --> 00:14:29.290
Pick whichever you want, but make it 
one that looks like a fast runner.

00:14:29.290 --> 00:14:31.350
No, I already have mine picked out.

00:14:31.800 --> 00:14:32.570
Moron!

00:14:33.470 --> 00:14:34.920
Parabellum!

00:14:35.480 --> 00:14:36.930
Is that your horse?

00:14:44.340 --> 00:14:46.870
Looks like they're not gonna let 
us leave so easily after all...

00:14:47.820 --> 00:14:49.360
So it would seem.

00:14:49.360 --> 00:14:49.950
Let's go!

00:14:49.950 --> 00:14:50.780
Right!

00:15:07.640 --> 00:15:10.880
Come on, you're making me look like a fool.

00:15:11.930 --> 00:15:12.760
Stand under the umbrella.

00:15:12.760 --> 00:15:14.290
There's no reason.

00:15:14.290 --> 00:15:18.000
Getting wet causes no harm 
to the body of a Peacemaker.

00:15:18.000 --> 00:15:18.850
Do it anyway.

00:15:27.200 --> 00:15:28.280
You're getting wet.

00:15:28.660 --> 00:15:30.340
If your present condition continues,

00:15:30.340 --> 00:15:32.160
your body temperature will drop.

00:15:32.160 --> 00:15:33.030
Just shut up.

00:15:54.680 --> 00:15:56.700
This isn't working... Take the reins!

00:15:57.510 --> 00:15:58.920
They're faster than we are.

00:15:58.920 --> 00:16:00.270
They're going to catch up.

00:16:00.270 --> 00:16:01.140
You go back without me.

00:16:02.050 --> 00:16:04.600
If we lead them back with us, 
all this will be for nothing!

00:16:04.600 --> 00:16:05.770
Take them!

00:16:05.770 --> 00:16:08.320
I'll catch up with you! Tell that to Pamela!

00:16:08.320 --> 00:16:10.240
I'll hold them off here.

00:16:10.240 --> 00:16:11.240
But I can help...

00:16:11.240 --> 00:16:12.030
You idiot!

00:16:12.510 --> 00:16:14.990
Isn't it a knight's duty 
to protect his princess?!

00:16:16.450 --> 00:16:17.200
Yes, but...

00:16:17.200 --> 00:16:20.620
Tell me, who's going to 
protect Pamela? Say it!

00:16:21.260 --> 00:16:22.120
I will...

00:16:22.120 --> 00:16:24.250
I can't hear you! Say it like you believe it!

00:16:24.250 --> 00:16:25.170
I will!

00:16:25.330 --> 00:16:26.130
Then protect her!

00:16:26.130 --> 00:16:27.090
Yes, sir!

00:16:42.910 --> 00:16:46.150
Run for it! Hurry!

00:16:46.900 --> 00:16:48.360
Get going!

00:17:02.550 --> 00:17:04.210
Miss Pamela!

00:17:06.210 --> 00:17:09.170
Get on! You, too, Miss Winia! Hurry!

00:17:17.510 --> 00:17:19.260
Hey, where's Furet?

00:17:19.260 --> 00:17:21.060
He'll catch up with us later!

00:18:05.100 --> 00:18:06.210
That's enough.

00:18:07.220 --> 00:18:10.440
You know what happens to people 
who defy the kingdom...

00:18:11.460 --> 00:18:13.440
Why did you do it?

00:18:35.300 --> 00:18:37.510
Damn it...

00:18:46.020 --> 00:18:47.180
Crap...

00:18:53.250 --> 00:18:54.740
Damn it...

00:19:31.090 --> 00:19:34.020
He must've been trying to go somewhere.

00:19:34.680 --> 00:19:36.030
Go where?

00:19:36.030 --> 00:19:39.870
This man's life signs have already ceased.

00:19:40.560 --> 00:19:43.510
Wherever it was that he was trying to go,

00:19:43.510 --> 00:19:45.960
he doesn't need to go there now.

00:19:46.830 --> 00:19:50.340
He can't go, even if he wants to.

00:19:50.340 --> 00:19:53.040
Unless somebody tells him that, he'll 
never be able to rest in peace.

00:20:09.610 --> 00:20:11.140
Leopold...

00:20:11.710 --> 00:20:12.390
Yes?

00:20:14.740 --> 00:20:17.400
You haven't been able to 
look me in the eye. Why?

00:20:20.390 --> 00:20:22.380
Furet's going to come, isn't he?

00:20:28.700 --> 00:20:30.790
I'm gonna go back for Furet.

00:20:30.790 --> 00:20:33.000
You can't, Miss Pamela!

00:20:33.000 --> 00:20:34.750
Let go!

00:20:34.750 --> 00:20:36.410
Let go of me!

00:20:49.490 --> 00:20:51.100
Who are you?!

00:21:16.580 --> 00:21:21.730
<i>A blessing of rain falls quietly. (Falls.)</i>

00:21:21.730 --> 00:21:27.050
<i>Droplets of my love, 
which fall for someone...</i>

00:21:27.050 --> 00:21:34.230
<i>who is still waiting in a land far away.</i>

00:21:34.230 --> 00:21:40.020
<i>The morning wind blows, caressing 
my cheek. (What was that...)</i>

00:21:40.020 --> 00:21:45.150
<i>Did you feel something, feel something 
just now? (...on my cheek?)</i>

00:21:45.150 --> 00:21:48.320
<i>It goes up to the one and only sky... 
(More certain than anything.)</i>

00:21:48.320 --> 00:21:53.370
<i>a sky which has a fixed, certain meaning.</i>

00:21:53.370 --> 00:21:59.920
<i>I come to a stop in the shadow 
of clouds that chase after me.</i>

00:21:59.920 --> 00:22:03.380
<i>This journey of the heart 
that I wish to gaze upon...</i>

00:22:03.380 --> 00:22:06.590
<i>goes on forever and goes on forever.</i>

00:22:06.590 --> 00:22:13.220
<i>One day I will chance upon the 
voice I've not heard in so long.</i>

00:22:13.220 --> 00:22:15.180
<i>Alainn la-li-la.</i>

00:22:15.180 --> 00:22:19.900
<i>At last the ship sets sail, sets sail. 
(The ship glides on forever...)</i>

00:22:19.900 --> 00:22:25.190
<i>Yes, believe in this wide world... 
(...to the edge of seas unknown.)</i>

00:22:25.190 --> 00:22:28.530
<i>and go off into the distance.</i>

00:22:28.530 --> 00:22:32.630
<i>And onwards into the future.</i>

00:22:33.450 --> 00:22:46.460
"Next Time"

00:22:34.180 --> 00:22:35.950
Pacifica, captured by Chris' unit,

00:22:35.950 --> 00:22:37.960
is locked away in the capital's dungeon.

00:22:37.960 --> 00:22:41.580
It's a dank, lonely, cramped, dark, and 
smelly place that's unpleasant to be in.

00:22:41.580 --> 00:22:43.310
Pacifica, who is lonely and in low spirits,

00:22:43.310 --> 00:22:45.130
realizes that someone is 
in the cell next door.

00:22:45.130 --> 00:22:47.300
Why do you suppose this person 
was thrown in the dungeon?

00:22:47.300 --> 00:22:48.540
Next time on <i>Scrapped Princess</i>,

00:22:48.540 --> 00:22:49.630
"Aria of a Mother's Sorrow."

00:22:49.630 --> 00:22:50.470
Please tune in!
